{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"catapult","model_identifier":"catapult","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## catapult\n\nTorsion catapult (E3).\n\n- Cubes: 59 (12 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -21.0..21.0, y 0.0..52.0, z -69.5..53.0 (size 42.0 x 52.0 x 122.5 u = 118 x 146 x 345 cm).\nTorsion catapult: a heavy rectangular oak frame (3 m = 122 u long with the tongue, 42 u wide) on four solid plank wheels with iron tyres (0.5 m), a twisted sinew skein between iron washers at the front (with tensioning levers), two braced uprights carrying a padded crossbar, a 1.5 m throwing arm with an iron-rimmed cup, a rear winch (rope drum, two iron ratchet wheels and crank handles) and a team-colour stripe along both side beams. Faces -Z (it throws forward). 2 m tall with the arm up (70 u at the slam).\n\n**Hit box:** one box 42 x 30 x 104 u (frame, from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 1) plus, if needed, a second box 26 x 52 x 8 at z = -10 for the uprights.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `frame` (pivot on the ground under the front axle, so the slam rocks the rear up) > `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` (axle pivots), `uprights` (pivot at their feet), `arm` (pivot in the skein: pitch +87 = vertical against the pad), `winch` (drum + ratchet wheels + handles).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the tongue ring (front); `slot_crew_1` at the right winch handle (rear), facing -X... i.e. turned toward the machine; `slot_crew_2` on the left beside the arm, facing +X. Both on the ground, children of `root`.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): wheels turn once per 1.50 s (circumference 53.4 u), travel toward -Z.\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.24 s (release: spawn the stone at the cup, arm passing ~60 deg); the arm slams the pad at 0.30 s, bounces and rests up against it; the frame rocks (rear lifts 3 deg) and settles by 1.0 s. `fire` ends with the arm UP: play `reload` next. `reload` 4.0 s: the arm is winched down in 8 ratchet steps while the drum and ratchet wheels make two turns; key 4.0 s (cocked, ready to load). `idle` = cocked arm with a faint creak. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with a wobbling rear-left wheel. `destroyed` holds: both front wheels break off and fall flat, the nose of the frame drops to the ground (pivoting on the rear wheels), the uprights topple backward and the arm snaps sideways.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 1.5 | loop |\n| `fire` | 2.2 | once |\n| `reload` | 4 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 2 | hold |\n"},"description":"## catapult\n\nTorsion catapult (E3).\n\n- Cubes: 59 (12 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -21.0..21.0, y 0.0..52.0, z -69.5..53.0 (size 42.0 x 52.0 x 122.5 u = 118 x 146 x 345 cm).\nTorsion catapult: a heavy rectangular oak frame (3 m = 122 u long with the tongue, 42 u wide) on four solid plank wheels with iron tyres (0.5 m), a twisted sinew skein between iron washers at the front (with tensioning levers), two braced uprights carrying a padded crossbar, a 1.5 m throwing arm with an iron-rimmed cup, a rear winch (rope drum, two iron ratchet wheels and crank handles) and a team-colour stripe along both side beams. Faces -Z (it throws forward). 2 m tall with the arm up (70 u at the slam).\n\n**Hit box:** one box 42 x 30 x 104 u (frame, from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 1) plus, if needed, a second box 26 x 52 x 8 at z = -10 for the uprights.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `frame` (pivot on the ground under the front axle, so the slam rocks the rear up) > `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` (axle pivots), `uprights` (pivot at their feet), `arm` (pivot in the skein: pitch +87 = vertical against the pad), `winch` (drum + ratchet wheels + handles).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the tongue ring (front); `slot_crew_1` at the right winch handle (rear), facing -X... i.e. turned toward the machine; `slot_crew_2` on the left beside the arm, facing +X. Both on the ground, children of `root`.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): wheels turn once per 1.50 s (circumference 53.4 u), travel toward -Z.\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.24 s (release: spawn the stone at the cup, arm passing ~60 deg); the arm slams the pad at 0.30 s, bounces and rests up against it; the frame rocks (rear lifts 3 deg) and settles by 1.0 s. `fire` ends with the arm UP: play `reload` next. `reload` 4.0 s: the arm is winched down in 8 ratchet steps while the drum and ratchet wheels make two turns; key 4.0 s (cocked, ready to load). `idle` = cocked arm with a faint creak. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with a wobbling rear-left wheel. `destroyed` holds: both front wheels break off and fall flat, the nose of the frame drops to the ground (pivoting on the rear wheels), the uprights topple backward and the arm snaps sideways.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 1.5 | loop |\n| `fire` | 2.2 | once |\n| `reload` | 4 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 2 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":256,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"beam_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[11.5,9.5,-50.0],"to":[16.5,16.0,50.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,-36.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[176,140,181.0,146.5],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[101,125,201.0,131.5],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[181,140,186.0,146.5],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,133,100.0,139.5],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,5.0,100.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[5,0,10.0,100.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"e9c66afe-f2e7-52e5-912d-e7d34f90abe1"},{"name":"team_stripe_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[16.4,12.0,-40.0],"to":[16.7,13.5,4